# Implementation Plan — Font Size Consistency and Aesthetic Optimization

This plan outlines the steps to standardize typography and font sizes across the entire ERP web application. By replacing arbitrary, hardcoded inline and stylesheet-specific font sizes with a centralized typography scale of CSS variables, we will ensure that text displays consistently, professionally, and beautifully on every page.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Typography Scale Introduction**
> We are proposing a standard typographic scale based on CSS variables inside the global [index.css](file:///d:/OneWebPC/OneDrive/ERP%20for%20U/src/index.css). 
> - `--font-size-xs`: `0.75rem` (12px) - for badges, metadata, captions, tooltips.
> - `--font-size-sm`: `0.875rem` (14px) - for table contents, helper text, form inputs, secondary buttons.
> - `--font-size-base`: `1rem` (16px) - for standard body text, primary labels, main buttons.
> - `--font-size-md`: `1.125rem` (18px) - for card headers, view subheaders.
> - `--font-size-lg`: `1.25rem` (20px) - for modal titles, primary section headers.
> - `--font-size-xl`: `1.5rem` (24px) - for module names, secondary page titles.
> - `--font-size-2xl`: `1.75rem` (28px) - for main view headings, metric values.
> - `--font-size-3xl`: `2.25rem` (36px) - for large displays, hero headers.

> [!TIP]
> **Helper Utility Classes**
> We will also introduce utility classes like `.text-sm` and `.text-md` which map directly to these variables. This allows us to write cleaner JSX and easily maintain spacing or scale.

